   :gap/count 1
   :gap/adr "ADR-2608153000"
   ;; The docstring of `origin-tlds` says the observed set is deliberate because
   ;; "a repo under a TLD nobody has used here yet is reported as an undeclared
   ;; prefix, which surfaces it for a decision instead of silently absorbing
   ;; it." Measured: it is not reported. On 2026-08-15 the two new
   ;; ws-valueflo-* repositories appeared in NEITHER the conformant list nor
   ;; the misfiled list nor any undeclared-prefix list -- `classify` fell
   ;; through and they left the origin plane entirely. Declaring "ws" moved the
   ;; counts from 28/1266 to 30/1268, which is how the invisibility was found.
   ;;
   ;; This is the shape ADR-2608136000 is about: the check that COULD NOT
   ;; classify a name returned the same output as a check that classified it
   ;; and found no problem. Silence accumulated as green.
   ;;
   ;; The fix belongs in the script, not here: an origin-shaped name
   ;; (<head>-<rest>) whose head is not a declared TLD should be listed as
   ;; UNDECLARED-TLD rather than dropped. Recorded rather than done, because
   ;; the head token of a bare subject-plane name is indistinguishable from an
   ;; undeclared TLD without a rule for which heads are plausible TLDs, and
   ;; guessing that would flood the audit.
   :gap/note "declaring a TLD is currently the only way to make a name visible
              to the audit, so an unregistered authority TLD hides its repos
              instead of surfacing them."}

